.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Functions for working with stream targets (that is, FILE pointers)\&. 

\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP Logging to stream targets is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate writes to the stream\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to stream targets is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate writes to the stream\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to stream targets is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void stumpless_close_stream_target (const struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Closes a stream target\&. This function does NOT close the stream associated with the target\&. It does destroy all memory allocated for the target, including the target struct itself\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this target\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The stream target to close\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
