.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_stream_target (const char * name, FILE * stream)"

.PP
Opens a stream target for the given stream\&. Events logged to this target will be separated by a newline, just as with a file target\&. In fact, a stream target is equivalent to a file target with the difference being that the file must be opened and closed by the caller\&.
.PP
A stream target can also be useful for logging to other streams, such as stdout and stderr, which is not possible with a file target\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the target to open\&. This is only used for identification of the target\&.
.br
\fIstream\fP The stream to log events to\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

