.SS "void stumpless_set_severity_color (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target, enum \fBstumpless_severity\fP severity, const char * escape_code)"

.PP
Sets the ANSI escape code (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ANSI_escape_code) to be printed in a specific target when a log is made at some severity\&. It should be used with stdout or stderr as targets, since it is only for aesthetic purposes\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:escape_code\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that escape_code is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The name of the target for which to set the colors\&.
.br
\fIseverity\fP The severity code (LOG_ERR etc\&.) to which we set the specific color\&.
.br
\fIescape_code\fP The ANSI escape code representing the color\&. 
.RE
.PP

